	- add --replace/-r option; previously only --backup triggered in-place write
	- add --output-format/-o option to serialize set output in a different format than input
	- default get key to '.' (entire document) when no key argument is supplied
	(_write_file)
	- rewrite to write to a tempfile in the same directory, then rename, preserving original permissions
	- require an input filename; die if infile is absent or stdin
	- restore backup on failure; refuse to overwrite an existing backup file
	(_fetch_data)
	- add format auto-detection: .xml extension and Bedrock XML markup recognized before JSON/YAML fallback
	- require top-level document to be a hash or array; die with accumulated parse errors otherwise
	- store resolved input_format for use by _serialize
	(_xml_data): new; lazy-loads Bedrock::XML and parses Bedrock XML input via newFromString/devolve
	(_serialize): new; resolves output format from --output-format, input_format, or 'json' default; lazy-loads Bedrock::XML for XML output; uses local $Data::NestedKey::FORMAT to avoid global mutation
	(cmd_set): trigger _write_file when --replace or --backup is set; output via _serialize instead of as_string
	(init): validate both --format and --output-format; drop setting of global $Data::NestedKey::FORMAT here
	(main): add replace|r and output-format|o to option_specs
